  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/BAB26B">Definition <span data-tag="BAB26B">6.3.6.1</span>.</a>image of a geometric morphism Let $f: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a geometric morphism of $\infty $-topoi. The <em>image</em> of $f$ is defined to be the smallest full subcategory of $\calX $ which contains $f^{\ast } \calY $ and is stable under small colimits and finite limits. We will say that $f$ is <em>algebraic</em> if the image of $f$ coincides with $\calX $.algebraic morphism </p>
